stories, it's the truth!

260
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:57,607
I heard it with my own ears.

261
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:02,217
Clawdor is a pirate captain who weaseled
his way into your family's home.

262
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,417
So he could steal your fortune.

263
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:05,837
He's pretended to be your
butler for three years.

264
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,817
So he could kill you
and inherit your money?

265
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:10,320
What are you talking about, Usopp?

266
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:13,717
His crew is going to
raid the village at dawn.

267
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:16,565
And in the process, you're
going to get killed!

268
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:22,400
Clawdor's a very bad man!

269
00:14:22,640 --> 00:14:23,857
Your life is in danger!

270
00:14:23,940 --> 00:14:25,058
You have to escape!

271
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:30,660
He did treat you harshly earlier,
and I understand that you're hurt.

272
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:34,700
But lying like this, it's not like you!

273
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,320
Kaya, please!

274
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:39,129
I'm telling you the truth!

275
00:14:43,380 --> 00:14:46,100
I loved them. Every one. One.

276
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:51,840
All those lies you told me,
they brought joy to my heart.

277
00:14:52,080 --> 00:14:54,500
But this is just vengeful poison.

278
00:14:56,920 --> 00:14:58,800
Kaya, please, listen to me.

279
00:14:58,920 --> 00:15:01,437
I'm not just trying to
get back at Klahadore.

280
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:03,860
Why would you do that? It's wrong.

281
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:06,960
Kaya, I...

282
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:10,440
Miss Kaya, is everything okay up here?

283
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:16,797
Let's get out of here!

284
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:17,710
Right now!

285
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,118
Unhand her immediately, you villain!

286
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,060
Please trust me, Kaia.

287
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:27,026
You gotta get out of this village
before that butler gets back!

288
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,460
Stop it!

289
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:45,610
Come on!

290
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:54,954
I promise this will all make sense
tomorrow, but right now we need to go!

291
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:57,280
Kaya, please, please trust me!

292
00:16:05,180 --> 00:16:06,220
You're pathetic!

293
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:18,950
Leave Ms.

294
00:16:19,033 --> 00:16:20,274
Kai alone, you maniac!

295
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,550
No!

296
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:39,497
Don't let that lunatic get away!

297
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:42,756
He broke in and tried to
kidnap the lady of the house.

298
00:16:49,820 --> 00:16:52,200
Why why won't anyone believe me?

299
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:10,697
There, there, ma 'am.

300
00:17:10,780 --> 00:17:12,545
Everything's going to be fine.

301
00:17:28,540 --> 00:17:29,370
Captain!

302
00:17:32,980 --> 00:17:34,600
Hey, how's it going, guys?

303
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:36,440
Hey, Captain! What is that?

304
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:40,040
Wait, you're alive again?

305
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:41,410
Alive?

306
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:43,600
Yeah, and I had a pretty good nap.

307
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:45,477
He was sleeping the whole time.

308
00:17:45,560 --> 00:17:48,457
Captain, we heard all about those
pirates and their evil plan.

309
00:17:48,540 --> 00:17:52,317
We better hurry and warn the people in
the village so they have time to get away.

310
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,420
Warn the people?

311
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,160
You're pathetic.

312
00:18:00,940 --> 00:18:01,770
Stop it!

313
00:18:01,853 --> 00:18:04,035
We all know you're nothing but a liar.

314
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:06,490
Ah!

315
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:14,540
Well, obviously I'm lying like usual.

316
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:17,057
That butler made me so
mad with what he said.

317
00:18:17,140 --> 00:18:20,434
I thought I'd get him back
and say that he was a pirate.

318
00:18:21,540 --> 00:18:22,620
Oh, I get it.

319
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:25,073
You put the Straw Hat guy up to it, too.

320
00:18:30,300 --> 00:18:31,980
Hey, where are you going?

321
00:18:32,860 --> 00:18:36,160
Honestly, you've really
disappointed me. Yeah.

322
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:38,437
Even though that butler guy is a jerk,

323
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:40,517
I thought you were better
than lying to hurt someone

324
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:43,637
and I admired you for being
such a kind-hearted person.

325
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:47,160
And I think we respected
you this entire time.

326
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:48,320
Let's go home.

327
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,384
Yeah, it's supper time anyways.

328
00:18:57,480 --> 00:18:59,400
So, how come you lied to them?

329
00:18:59,860 --> 00:19:01,620
Because all I do is lie.

330
00:19:02,340 --> 00:19:04,937
There's no way anybody was
gonna believe what I had to say.

331
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:06,240
Why should they?

332
00:19:07,900 --> 00:19:11,097
Because what you were telling
them was the honest truth.

333
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:14,397
They are coming, and they're
going to level this whole town.

334
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:16,539
Yeah, but what am I supposed to do?

335
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:19,426
They'll think I'm lying
if I try to warn them.

336
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:24,462
Everyone in the village thinks that tomorrow's
just going to be another normal day.

337
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:27,417
They think I'm lying, and
that's all they need to think.

338
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:30,677
I'm going to stop those pirates
at the beach tomorrow myself.

339
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:33,320
This is all my fault
for being such a liar.

340
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:39,208
I don't care anymore if they drive me
away with brooms or shoot me in the arm.

341
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,677
This is my village.

342
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:43,197
It's my home.

343
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:45,140
And I love everyone in it.

344
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:50,140
I have to protect them.

345
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:53,037
You're a hell of a good guy.

346
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:55,837
Sending your cronies away
and going into battle alone.

347
00:19:55,920 --> 00:19:57,017
Just so you know.

348
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:59,637
I have dibs on all the
pirate treasure, you got it?

349
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,397
So you want a little help or what?

350
00:20:01,480 --> 00:20:04,880
You guys, you're gonna help
me fight all these pirates?

351
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:06,120
I don't get it.

352
00:20:06,440 --> 00:20:09,597
Well, you said there's a whole
bunch of bad guys, right?

353
00:20:09,680 --> 00:20:11,856
And you look scared out of your mind.

354
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:14,477
For your information,
I have nerves of steel.

355
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:16,937
I'm perfectly okay with tons of bad guys.

356
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:19,737
After all, you're looking at
the legendary Captain Usopp,

357
00:20:19,820 --> 00:20:21,644
brave warrior of the high seas.

358
00:20:24,620 --> 00:20:25,450
Damn it.

359
00:20:25,840 --> 00:20:27,417
All right, fine, I'm scared.

360
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:28,330
Why shouldn't I be?

361
00:20:28,413 --> 00:20:29,637
They're Captain Curl's men.

362
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,037
These guys mean business.

363
00:20:31,120 --> 00:20:34,237
I don't need pity if you
guys are sticking around cuz

364
00:20:34,320 --> 00:20:37,277
you pity me just leave I
don't need you laughing at me.

365
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:38,960
We're not laughing at you.

366
00:20:39,100 --> 00:20:41,394
We're helping because you are honorable

367
00:20:42,700 --> 00:20:45,465
You really think we risk
our lives out of pity?

368
00:21:07,820 --> 00:21:11,297
As a kid, I never stopped.

369
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:13,857
Searching for a great treasure.

370
00:21:13,940 --> 00:21:18,657
I had a map in my mind.

371
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:21,257
That I knew would lead me.

372
00:21:21,340 --> 00:21:25,457
I had to find my way to that place.

373
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:28,357
Before someone could beat me.

374
00:21:28,440 --> 00:21:32,557
The promised land was in my grasp.

375
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:35,240
And I wouldn't let go.

376
00:21:36,300 --> 00:21:38,997
La la la la.

377
00:21:39,080 --> 00:21:40,417
My only dream.

378
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:42,657
La la la la la.

379
00:21:42,740 --> 00:21:48,540
I won't stop chasing
it until it comes true.

380
00:21:50,340 --> 00:21:53,777
But the world ever changes.

381
00:21:53,860 --> 00:21:56,617
I call out your name.

382
00:21:56,700 --> 00:22:00,677
We could return to the time

383
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:03,817
when everything's the same.

384
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:10,477
As long as I'm with you,
my memories won't fade.

385
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:15,880
Waiting for that one true dream?
